.TH GPUBENCH-GUI 1 "September 2026" "GPUBench 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gpubench-gui \- Graphical interface for GPU compute and hardware ray tracing benchmarking
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gpubench-gui
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B GPUBench GUI
is the graphical interface for GPUBench, a cross-backend GPU compute and hardware ray tracing benchmark suite. It features real-time telemetry graphs (GPU clock, temperature, power, VRAM, activity), configurable test suites, visual parity inspection with split/diff/heatmap views, and analytical scorecard evaluations. Command line options can be supplied to preconfigure options or run benchmarks non-interactively.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display program version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-backend " \fIBACKEND\fR"
Select default compute backend: auto, vulkan, opencl, rocm.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-group ", " \-\-groups " \fINAMES\fR"
Benchmark group(s) to enable: compute, memory, graphics (combines raster & raytracing), raster, raytracing, system, all.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-benchmark ", " \-\-benchmarks ", " \-t ", " \-\-test " \fIBENCHMARKS\fR"
Specific benchmark(s) to enable (comma-separated). Supported identifiers include: fp32, fp64, dualissue, lds, indirect, fp16, bf16, fp8, fp6, fp4, int8, int4, membw, l0_cache, cache_latency_curve, pixelfill, rayrawtraversal, rayasbuild, rayintersect, rayanyhit, rayprocedural, rayscheduling, raydivergence, sysmembw, sysmemlatency, all.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-device " \fIDEVICES\fR"
Target GPU device index(es) (e.g., 0, 1, 0,1, dual, or all).
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-scene " \fISCENE\fR"
Pre-select Ray Tracing scene: showroom, indoor, outdoor, forest.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-res ", " \-\-resolution " \fIPRESET\fR"
Resolution preset: 720p, 1080p, 1440p, 4k, 8k, or custom WxH.
.TP
.BR \-\-ui-scale ", " \-\-scale " \fISCALE\fR"
Override UI DPI scaling factor (e.g., 1.0, 1.25, 1.5, 2.0).
.TP
.BR \-\-dump-renders ", " \-\-dump
Enable visual verification and dump comparison frames to disk.
.TP
.BR \-\-no-dump-renders ", " \-\-no-dump
Disable saving rendered output images to disk.
.TP
.BR \-\-auto-run ", " \-\-auto-start ", " \-\-run
Automatically begin benchmark execution immediately upon launch.
.TP
.BR \-\-exit-on-complete
Exit automatically when the benchmark run finishes.
.TP
.BR \-\-frames " \fICOUNT\fR"
Run for the specified number of frames and exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose
Enable verbose logging output.
.TP
.BR \-\-debug
Enable debug logging output.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Launch GUI with Vulkan backend, Ray Tracing group, and GPU 0 selected:
.B gpubench-gui \-k vulkan \-g raytracing \-d 0
.TP
Launch GUI with Compute and Memory benchmarks at 1080p:
.B gpubench-gui \-g compute,memory \-r 1080p
.TP
Run Ray Scheduling benchmark automatically and dump renders:
.B gpubench-gui \-b rayscheduling \-\-dump-renders \-\-auto-run
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gpubench (1)
